UA-SEA-RAFT
===========

This repository contains ONLY original code written for the project
"Uncertainty-Aware Adaptive Iteration Stopping for SEA-RAFT".

It contains NO source code copied from any third-party project.

The upstream optical-flow model, SEA-RAFT, is consumed as a git submodule at
`third_party/SEA-RAFT` and is licensed separately by its authors:

    SEA-RAFT: Simple, Efficient, Accurate RAFT for Optical Flow
    Yihan Wang, Lahav Lipson, Jia Deng (Princeton University)
    ECCV 2024 (Oral) - arXiv:2405.14793
    https://github.com/princeton-vl/SEA-RAFT
    License: BSD-3-Clause (see third_party/SEA-RAFT/LICENSE after init)

Nothing here modifies upstream files in place. The `scale` correction, the
five uncertainty read-outs, the stopping criterion, the latency model, the
threshold sweep and the risk certificate are all implemented in `ua_stop/`
and applied from the outside, through a wrapper. This is deliberate: it keeps
the licensing clean and makes every reported number reproducible against an
unmodified upstream commit.

Model weights (`MemorySlices/Tartan-C-T-TSKH-spring540x960-M`) are downloaded
at run time from the authors' Hugging Face repository and are NOT redistributed
here.

Datasets (KITTI-2015, MPI-Sintel, Spring, TartanAir) are NOT redistributed.
Each carries its own license and must be obtained from its official source.

If you use this code, please cite SEA-RAFT (see README.md for the BibTeX
entry) in addition to this repository.
